{"type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn9le10ob06re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn9le10ob06re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn9le10ob06re2img05.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0"}, {"image": "engenn9le10ob06re2img05.jpg", "text": "<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: Are you still at the fair?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Adam</span>: Yes. There are a few booths I've not visited yet. <br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: Okay. I have a few guidelines that will help you land a job. <br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Adam</span>: Go for it.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: Stand up while you're waiting. <br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Adam</span>: Could you expand on that?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: People are often asked to take a seat while they wait. Don't do it. What you want is to impress them and look more confident. You can only do this if you are on their level when you meet them. <br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Adam</span>: Ok. That's sound advice. What more? <br />", "id": 1, "time": "100"}, {"image": "engenn9le10ob06re2img06.jpg", "text": "<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: Don't speak too fast. <br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Adam</span>: Could you elaborate on that?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: You want to be intelligible. What you can do to avoid this is to breath slowly through your nose. This will help you lower your heart rate. <br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Adam</span>: Breathing is important. Got it. <br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: Be comfortable when you sit. <br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Adam</span>: Uh, could you shed some light on this?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: What I'm suggesting is to find a sitting position that suits you. What I usually do is sit straight and maybe lean forward a bit. You'll look more professional that way. <br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Adam</span>: Sitting is important, then. <br />", "id": 2, "time": "32000"}, {"image": "engenn9le10ob06re2img07.jpg", "text": "<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: Make sure you are eagerly listening.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Adam</span>: I am not a good listener. Could you be more specific?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: When we're trembling with fear, we tend to become bad listeners. What I find particularly useful is to take a deep breath, listen to your body and wear a smile. You'll make the interviewer feel special and demonstrate that you valued their question. <br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Adam</span>: Any more tips?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: Be thankful. <br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Adam</span>: Could you clarify that?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: What I've learned from my research is that one should thank everyone promptly. What you could do is send a thank-you e-mail after the interview. <br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Adam</span>: These are great tips, Kristi! I'm sure I'll do better on my next interview.<br />", "id": 3, "time": "68000"}]}}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can exchange complex information about work.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can deal with communication breakdowns. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about facts and courses of action.    ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What advice would you give someone before a job interview?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What works best? Why?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_atte