pe": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Identify and describe issues relating to money, in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts..", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le10ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " What Clauses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you use a\u00a0 <span class=\"italic\">what\u00a0,\u00a0that,</span> or\u00a0 <span class=\"italic\">who</span>\u00a0clause as the subject of a sentence, you have shifted the emphasis away from the words that sit in the subject position.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Look at these examples:<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Original Sentence</span><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">You want to impress them and look more confident. </span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Noun Clause Sentence</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\">What you want</span> is to impress them and look more confident. </span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "We call the first part of the sentence a phrase. If it is removed, the structure no longer makes sense: ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><strike>What </strike>you could do is send a thank-you e-mail after the interview.</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\"><strike>What</strike> I find particularly useful is to take a deep breath, listen to your body and wear a smile</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "This is how we form \u201cWhat\u201d clauses. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> subject / What-phrase</div> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">complement</div> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">What I'm suggesting<br/> What I usually do<br/> What I've learned from my research</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">is <br/> is <br/> is</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">to find a sitting position that suits you.<br/> sit straight and maybe lean forward a bit.<br/> one should thank everyone promptly. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Asking for Extension", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " Communication is a two-way street. It involves a lot of back and forth. Therefore, it is important to communicate when something is not clear to you or when you need more from the other speaker. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " Asking for an extension is important in many situations especially when the message being communicated is difficult or new in some way. Here are some ways you can ask for an extension.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Could you expand on that?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Could you elaborate on that?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Uh, could you shed some light on this?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Could you be more specific?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Could you clarify that?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to land a job", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to get a job", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: These tips will help you land a job.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le10ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when giving advice for a job interview.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "guidelines", "type": "name"}, {"content": "advice about how to do something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: These guidelines will help you with landing a job.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le10ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sound advice", "type": "name"}, {"content": "good, useful advice", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: That is sound advice. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le10ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "intelligible", "type": "name"}, {"content": "clear or simple enough to understand ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You want to be intelligible. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le10ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "shed some light", "type": "name"}, {"content": "provide new information that helps you understand something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Could you shed some light on this?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le10ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to tremble", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to shake because you are nervous, afraid or excited", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I was trembling with fear. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le10ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "eagerly", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be very enthusiastic about something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Make sure you are eagerly listening.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le10ob06aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "promptly", "type": "name"}, {"content": "immediately ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Make sure you thank everyone promptly. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le10ob06aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "You are going to help a friend prepare for an interview.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Go online and research job interview tips. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Choose 3 to 5 tips that you consider important. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Give your partner advice using What-phrases.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I research job interview tips.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I choose the most important tips.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give advice using What-clauses. ", "type": "text"}]}]}